{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aaweaver-actuary/tempo/pulls/226","id":4832632280,"node_id":"PR_kwDOUcYs_s8AAAABIAwd2A","html_url":"https://github.com/aaweaver-actuary/tempo/pull/226","diff_url":"https://github.com/aaweaver-actuary/tempo/pull/226.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/aaweaver-actuary/tempo/pull/226.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aaweaver-actuary/tempo/issues/226","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aaweaver-actuary/tempo/pulls/226/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aaweaver-actuary/tempo/pulls/226/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aaweaver-actuary/tempo/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aaweaver-actuary/tempo/issues/226/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aaweaver-actuary/tempo/statuses/8200e096d6a2b3475dba34f55c7ff381785be0a0","number":226,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Extract A1 scheduling store using the existing owned connection (#204)","user":{"login":"aaweaver-actuary","id":53792857,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzNzkyODU3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53792857?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaweaver-actuary","html_url":"https://github.com/aaweaver-actuary","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaweaver-actuary/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaweaver-actuary/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaweaver-actuary/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaweaver-actuary/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaweaver-actuary/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaweaver-actuary/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaweaver-actuary/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaweaver-actuary/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaweaver-actuary/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Problem and behavior\n\nScheduling orchestration currently embeds SQL for source/history/card/seed effects. This PR implements **A1 only** from #204 and #217: five typed capabilities behind an adapter borrowing the existing owned connection, with infrastructure-free application tests. The scheduling wrapper and response remain compatible; the adapter never opens a connection or commits.\n\nSource replay still returns current card facts, while gateway/logical receipt replay remains unchanged. Clock/date/source inputs and history/seed maturity are explicit. Existing wrapper follow-ups remain in the caller transaction. No schema/public API changes. `main.py`, gateway, review commands and queue helpers are unchanged. #220 owns queue extraction; **#224 remains separate and incomplete**.\n\n## Regression protection and risk\n\nMedium–high persistence risk despite a narrow extraction: ordering, original clocks, archived/current-card source replay, invalidated history, seed padding, borrowed-connection follow-ups and owner rollback. New regular-suite fake-store/SQLite tests and two native proofs cover these boundaries; native proofs are wired through the existing queue-attempt durability hook. Existing expectations are unchanged. See `tests/REGRESSIONS.md` and `docs/architecture/ci-isolation/scheduling-store-a1.md`.\n\n## Evidence and pending qualification\n\nSource main: `3f7332399796366eb32f9fcb5e1b5c678a5b1562`.\nImplementation head: `d26ef448dd5b4791a37d0d1f4c765574ebad9061`.\nLocal environment: macOS arm64, CPython 3.14.8; product native runner uses pinned Docker prerequisites.\n\n- Pre-extraction `make python-file FILE=backend/tests/test_scheduling_review_store.py`: 5 characterization cases passed, 0.55s pytest. The first new fixture expectation was corrected to observed original FSRS behavior before any product edit; existing expectations were not changed.\n- Two new test files: 23 passed, 0.88s pytest.\n- Explicit pytest selection covering the two new files, phone offline, prepared continuation, queue recovery/issuance, guided/native-guided contracts, opening graph, real-game feedback and defense persistence: 218 passed, 61.08s pytest. This preceded the final fresh-interpreter guard expansion.\n- Explicit pytest selection covering the final application guard, studies, study durability, study-only, game adaptation, services and card deletion: 81 passed, 12.91s pytest / 13.61s wall.\n- `node --test tests/runner/postgres-test-speedups.test.mjs`: 67 passed, 2.655s runner.\n- `git diff --check`: passed. Python compilation passed for the expanded native hook.\n\n`make docker-durability` is running on the clean implementation commit; new rollback/concurrent replay, browser specs and exact-candidate FULL CI evidence are pending. Focused local evidence does not establish full qualification. CI owns complete candidate validation; `ci:full` explicitly requests it. Head/base/integration SHAs and run links will be recorded after qualification.\n\n#146 authoritative enqueue and #191 outbox settlement stay separate; their shared identity/continuation contracts are preserved. No dependency implementation is transplanted into A1.\n\n## Rollback and resources\n\nRevert extraction commits; unchanged schemas/history/receipts/pending intents remain compatible. No deployment or merge is requested. Task-owned disposable runner resources only; live study and other tasks are untouched. Evidence is preserved under dated root `test-results/`; verified teardown and checkout preservation/removal will be recorded at handoff.\n\nCloses #204 when the complete A1 criteria are qualified and merged. References #217, #192, #220 and #224.\n\n## Summary by Sourcery\n\nExtract scheduling review persistence behind a typed adapter that borrows the caller-owned connection while preserving existing behavior and transaction boundaries.\n\nNew Features:\n- Introduce a typed scheduling application layer and owned-connection store adapter for review scheduling persistence.\n\nBug Fixes:\n- Preserve source replay, maturity calculation, rollback, and borrowed-connection behavior while extracting scheduling persistence.\n\nEnhancements:\n- Separate scheduling decisions from SQL persistence while retaining the existing wrapper contract and transaction ownership.\n- Make completion timing, review dates, source identity, history, and seed maturity inputs explicit.\n\nCI:\n- Add native durability coverage for scheduling rollback, concurrent replay, receipt failures, and exactly-once queue effects.\n\nDocumentation:\n- Document the A1 scheduling-store boundary, transaction ownership, compatibility guarantees, and qualification requirements.\n\nTests:\n- Add infrastructure-free application tests and SQLite adapter characterization tests covering ordering, replay, maturity, invalid history, rollback, and follow-ups.","labels":[{"id":12610267999,"node_id":"LA_kwDOUcYs_s8AAAAC76FrXw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aaweaver-actuary/tempo/labels/ci:full","name":"ci:full","description":"Run complete verification on a draft; development evidence does not qualify it for merging.","color":"19794b","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-12T17:08:48Z","updated_at":"2026-10-12T17:11:54Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"10994073fa5dcf885d807d9d2dc5b6a508a8cd36","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"aaweaver-actuary:codex/issue-204-scheduling-store","ref":"codex/issue-204-scheduling-store","repo":{"id":1371942142,"node_id":"R_kgDOUcYs_g","name":"tempo","full_name":"aaweaver-actuary/tempo","owner":{"login":"aaweaver-actuary","id":53792857,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzNzkyODU3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53792857?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaweaver-actuary","html_url":"https://git